Q: Can you use some kind of wildcard character in URL redirects in Joomla&#39;s Redirect component? A: <p>You can not use Joomla redirect component for bulk URL redirect. You can use a custom system plugin for the same. Refer to this documentation to learn how you can create custom Joomla plugins - <a href="https://docs.joomla.org/J3.x:Creating_a_Plugin_for_Joomla" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://docs.joomla.org/J3.x:Creating_a_Plugin_for_Joomla</a></p>
<p>Here are the example codes of the plugin -</p>
<p><strong>customredirect.php</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

defined ('_JEXEC') or die;

class plgSystemCustomRedirect extends JPlugin
{
    /**
     * Application object.
     *
     * @var    JApplicationCms
     */
    protected $app;

    /**
     * Match and redirect to new urls
     *
     * @return  void
     */
    public function onAfterRoute()
    {
        $doc = $this-&gt;app-&gt;getDocument();

        if (!$this-&gt;app-&gt;isClient('site') || $doc-&gt;getType() !== 'html')
        {
            return;
        }

        $url     = JUri::getInstance()-&gt;toString(array('scheme', 'host', 'port', 'path', 'query', 'fragment'));
        $find    = JUri::base() . 'about/news/entry/';
        $replace = JUri::base() . 'news/entry/';

        if (strpos($url, $find) === 0 &amp;&amp; strlen($url) &gt; strlen($find))
        {
            $newUrl = str_replace($find, $replace, $url);

            $this-&gt;app-&gt;redirect($newUrl);
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>customredirect.xml</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;extension version=&quot;3.5&quot; type=&quot;plugin&quot; group=&quot;system&quot; method=&quot;upgrade&quot;&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;System - Custom Redirect&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;author&gt;Jumbo&lt;/author&gt;
    &lt;creationDate&gt;May 2021&lt;/creationDate&gt;
    &lt;license&gt;GNU General Public License version 2 or later; see LICENSE.txt&lt;/license&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;1.0&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;files&gt;
        &lt;filename plugin=&quot;customredirect&quot;&gt;customredirect.php&lt;/filename&gt;
    &lt;/files&gt;
&lt;/extension&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How to get host name with port from a http or https request A: <p><strong>Proxy</strong></p>
<p>Make sure the proxy server sends the defacto standard `X-Forwarded-Proto` http header. Apache does this by default.</p>
<p><strong>Application Server</strong></p>
<p>Not every application server honors this header automatically.</p>
<p>If you are using glassfish application server behind a proxy you also need to tell glassfish what the scheme mapping name in the proxy header is for the glassfish domain. You do this in the domain config file `config/config.xml` in the domain folder of your glassfish installation:</p>
<p>Add <code>scheme-mapping=</code><em><code>&quot;X-Forwarded-Proto&quot;</code></em> to the http-listener protocol. This cannot be done in admin console as far as i know.</p>
<p><strong>Example</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;protocols&gt;
          &lt;protocol name=&quot;http-listener-1&quot;&gt;
            &lt;http xpowered-by=&quot;false&quot; compressable-mime-type=&quot;text/html,text/xml,text/css,text/plain,text/javascript,application/javascript,application/json,image/svg+xml&quot; max-connections=&quot;1024&quot; default-virtual-server=&quot;server&quot; scheme-mapping=&quot;X-Forwarded-Proto&quot;&gt;
              &lt;file-cache max-cache-size-bytes=&quot;104857600&quot; max-age-seconds=&quot;14400&quot; max-files-count=&quot;2048&quot; enabled=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;
            &lt;/http&gt;
          &lt;/protocol&gt;
&lt;/protocols&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: replace karaf feature through features.xml A: <p>I've just checked with fresh Karaf 4.4.7 and added CXF features using:</p>
<pre><code>karaf@root()&gt; feature:repo-add cxf
Adding feature url mvn:org.apache.cxf.karaf/apache-cxf/RELEASE/xml/features
</code></pre>
<p>then installed <code>cxf-http</code> feature and got this bundle installed:</p>
<pre><code>59 │ Active   │  40 │ 3.6.10             │ mvn:org.apache.cxf/cxf-rt-transports-http/3.6.10
</code></pre>
<p>note start-level 40 and version 3.6.10 (it's because of <code>RELEASE</code> and what's available in <a href="https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/apache/cxf/karaf/apache-cxf/maven-metadata.xml" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/apache/cxf/karaf/apache-cxf/maven-metadata.xml</a>).</p>
<p>Then I've added your snippet to <code>etc/org.apache.karaf.features.xml</code> and of course it didn't work - because versions didn't match (3.5.5 vs 3.6.10).</p>
<p>So then I used this <code>etc/org.apache.karaf.features.xml</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;featuresProcessing xmlns=&quot;http://karaf.apache.org/xmlns/features-processing/v1.0.0&quot;
    xmlns:f=&quot;http://karaf.apache.org/xmlns/features/v1.6.0&quot;&gt;

    &lt;!-- you can eventually blacklist features repositories, features, or even bundle here, to exclude from resolution --&gt;
    &lt;!-- &lt;blacklistedRepositories/&gt; --&gt;
    &lt;featureReplacements&gt;
        &lt;replacement mode=&quot;replace&quot;&gt;
            &lt;feature name=&quot;cxf-http&quot; version=&quot;3.6.10&quot;&gt;
                &lt;f:feature version=&quot;3.6.10&quot;&gt;cxf-core&lt;/f:feature&gt;
                &lt;f:feature&gt;http&lt;/f:feature&gt;
                &lt;f:bundle start=&quot;false&quot; start-level=&quot;100&quot;&gt;mvn:org.apache.cxf/cxf-rt-transports-http/3.6.10&lt;/f:bundle&gt;
            &lt;/feature&gt;
        &lt;/replacement&gt;
    &lt;/featureReplacements&gt;

&lt;/featuresProcessing&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Note version 3.6.10, changed <code>start-level</code> and <code>start</code> attributes.</p>
<p>After uninstalling <code>cxf-http</code>, then calling <code>feature:refresh</code> then <code>feature:install -v cxf-http</code> again, I got:</p>
<pre><code>karaf@root()&gt; la -l | grep cxf-rt-transport
 97 │ Resolved │ 100 │ 3.6.10             │ mvn:org.apache.cxf/cxf-rt-transports-http/3.6.10
</code></pre>
<p>So I got changed <code>start-level</code> (100) and the bundle is not started.</p>
<p>Mind that there's another CXF feature which includes this bundle - <code>cxf-http-client</code>.</p>
